title: Payers › Documents › Try it on a case
route: /payers/cardinal?tab=documents
intro: 'Try it on a case' lets Reader read a chart against this payer's list. The chart is either a sample chart for a case still in 'Preparing', or text pasted into 'Paste chart text'. It is read only and sends nothing. A document only counts as missing when the payer's list actually asks for it.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Look at the card 'Try it on a case'\nright of the document list\nCheck a chart against this list"
decision hc "Is any case in 'Preparing'?"
toast nc "Menu shows 'No cases to check'"
process df "Case starts as the first 'Preparing' case for this payer,\nelse the first 'Preparing' case at all\nCardinal: I-2207"
input pk "Pick a 'Case'\nR-1042 · J.M., 34 (Residential 3.5)\nI-2207 · T.R., 29 (IOP)\nR-0988, R-1101, I-2262"
input pt "Type or paste in 'Paste chart text' (optional)\nHint: with text here, Reader checks it against the level\nof care list on the left instead of the case's chart"
process clr "Picking a case or changing the text\nclears any earlier result"
decision dt "Is there pasted text?\nBlank or spaces only counts as none"
decision dg "Is there a case or pasted text?"
endx xnc "'Check this chart' stays greyed out\nPaste text, or wait for a case to be prepared"
click ck "Click 'Check this chart'"
process busy "Button reads 'Reader is reading the chart' with a spinner"
agent rd "Reader reads the chart\n(demo: about 2 seconds, scripted)"
decision lv "Still on Payers after 2 seconds?"
endx drop "Result dropped"

group gC "A case's sample chart"
  process lc "'Level of care' switches to the case's program\nand the list on the left shows that list"
  process mt "Match the chart's known gaps against this payer's list\nA gap counts only if a list title contains it\nThe case's own payer does not matter"
  process gp "Sample charts lack\nR-1042: therapy note\nI-2207: attendance record, remaining treatment goals\nR-1101: urine drug screen, nursing note with withdrawal scale\nR-0988 and I-2262: nothing"
endgroup

group gT "Pasted text"
  process pl "Uses the level of care shown on the left\nThe chosen case is not used"
  process kw "Keyword check, the same text always gives the same answer\nA document is found when the text uses its name or a usual word\nfor it: CIWA or COWS for the withdrawal scale, UDS for the urine screen, h&p\nA document someone added is found when all its own words appear"
endgroup

decision dn "Is anything still needed?"
toast r1 "Ochre banner '5 of 6 ready'\nStill needed: an attendance record for the last 14 days.\nCardinal usually asks for it.\nA long list shows four, then 'and N more'"
toast r0 "Green banner '9 of 9 ready'\nNothing is missing. Reader found every document\nin the chart (or 'in the text')."
toast ft1 "'Checked I-2207 against Cardinal's IOP list.'\nLink 'Open the request'"
toast ft2 "'Checked the pasted text against Cardinal's IOP list, by keyword.'\nNo link: no case was used"
click ol "Click 'Open the request'"
goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Open a request"
process why "Edit the list and check again to see it change\nCardinal's list asks for 'Remaining treatment goals' only after\nits criteria change is updated, so I-2207 then reads '5 of 7 ready'"
toast info "'New case checks documents against this same list.\nPasted text is matched by keyword, so a document that\nis named differently can be missed.'"
goto g2 "Continues in: Payers › Documents › Edit the list"
goto g3 "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Medical records › The checklist and Continue"

s1 --> hc
hc -->|No| nc --> pt
hc -->|Yes| df --> pk --> pt
pt --> clr --> dg
dg -->|No| xnc
dg -->|Yes| ck --> busy --> rd --> lv
lv -->|No| drop
lv -->|Yes| dt
dt -->|Yes, the text is read| pl --> kw --> dn
dt -->|No, the case's chart is read| lc --> mt --> dn
mt -.-> gp
dn -->|Yes| r1
dn -->|No| r0
r1 --> ft1
r0 --> ft1
kw -.-> ft2
ft1 --> ol --> g1
ft1 --> why --> g2
s1 -.-> info
info -.-> g3
